<tbody><tr><td style="border-style:none"><div style="font-size:85%"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix_Suns_Arena" title="Phoenix Suns Arena" class="mw-redirect">Phoenix Suns Arena</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix,_Arizona" title="Phoenix, Arizona">Phoenix, Arizona</a><br/><b>Attendance:</b> 16,557<br/><b>Referees:</b> 
<ul><li>No. 8 Marc Davis</li>
<li>No. 58 Josh Tiven</li>
<li>No. 26 Pat Fraher</li></ul></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAWk"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Chris_Paul_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAWo"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Chris_Paul_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Chris_Paul_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Chris_Paul_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Chris_Paul_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Chris_Paul_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1734" data-file-height="2129" data-file-type="bitmap" height="233" width="190" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwAWs"/></a><figcaption id="mwAWw">In his finals debut, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Paul" title="Chris Paul" id="mwAW0">Chris Paul</a> scored a game-high 32 points, including 16 in the third quarter.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAW4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Paul" title="Chris Paul" id="mwAW8">Chris Paul</a> scored 32 points and had nine <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assist_(basketball)" title="Assist (basketball)" id="mwAXA">assists</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devin_Booker" title="Devin Booker" id="mwAXE">Devin Booker</a> added 27 points to lead Phoenix to a 118–105 win over Milwaukee. After he opened the third quarter with a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jump_shot_(basketball)" title="Jump shot (basketball)" id="mwAXI">jump shot</a> for the first double-digit lead of the game, Paul later scored eight straight points for the Suns and scored 16 overall in the quarter. Phoenix led 88–68 with 2:20 remaining in the quarter after Paul passed to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deandre_Ayton" title="Deandre Ayton" id="mwAXM">Deandre Ayton</a>, who was fouled and made two <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_throw" title="Free throw" id="mwAXQ">free throws</a>.<sup about="#mwt95" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07062021_21-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07062021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07062021-21" id="mwAXU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXc">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXg">]</span></span></a></sup> In his return from his knee injury, Bucks star <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giannis_Antetokounmpo" title="Giannis Antetokounmpo" id="mwAXk">Giannis Antetokounmpo</a> returned and had 20 points, 17 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebound_(basketball)" title="Rebound (basketball)" id="mwAXo">rebounds</a> in limited minutes due to foul trouble,<sup about="#mwt98" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07062021_21-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07062021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ap_07062021-21"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07062021-21" id="mwAXs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX0">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX4">]</span></span></a></sup> and made a chase-down <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Block_(basketball)" title="Block (basketball)" id="mwAX8">block</a> of a layup attempt by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikal_Bridges" title="Mikal Bridges" id="mwAYA">Mikal Bridges</a> that was reminiscent of "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Block_(basketball)" title="The Block (basketball)" id="mwAYE">The Block</a>" by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LeBron_James" title="LeBron James" id="mwAYI">LeBron James</a> on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andre_Iguodala" title="Andre Iguodala" id="mwAYM">Andre Iguodala</a> in Game 7 of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2016_NBA_Finals" title="2016 NBA Finals" id="mwAYQ">2016 Finals</a>.<sup about="#mwt99" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07072021_28-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07072021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07072021-28" id="mwAYU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYc">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYg">]</span></span></a></sup> Antetokounmpo's availability was not confirmed until almost an hour before <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jump_ball" title="Jump ball" id="mwAYk">tip-off</a>, and he played with few signs of injury.<sup about="#mwt102" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-29" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-29"}}'><a href="#cite_note-29" id="mwAYo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYw">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAY0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAY4">Milwaukee pulled to within seven points midway through the fourth quarter, but Paul passed to Booker for a 3-pointer and then <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steal_(basketball)" title="Steal (basketball)" id="mwAY8">stole</a> the ball from the Bucks' <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khris_Middleton" title="Khris Middleton" id="mwAZA">Khris Middleton</a> and hit a jumper to extend the lead to 106–94. Ayton finished the game with 22 points and 19 rebounds for Phoenix.<sup about="#mwt103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07062021_21-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07062021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07062021-21" id="mwAZE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZM">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Middleton scored 29 on 26 shots for the Bucks, but did not attempt a free throw. Teammate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jrue_Holiday" title="Jrue Holiday" id="mwAZU">Jrue Holiday</a> shot just 4 for 14. Milwaukee center <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brook_Lopez" title="Brook Lopez" id="mwAZY">Brook Lopez</a> was targeted on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Switch_(basketball)" title="Switch (basketball)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAZc">switches</a> by the Suns, and he was on the bench for most of the second half while Antetokounmpo played center.<sup about="#mwt106" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07072021_28-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07072021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-abrams_07072021-28"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07072021-28" id="mwAZg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZo">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAZw">The Suns had 26 free throw attempts in the game, 10 more than the Bucks.<sup about="#mwt109" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bontemps_07082021_30-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bontemps_07082021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-bontemps_07082021-30"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bontemps_07082021-30" id="mwAZ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ8">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaA">]</span></span></a></sup> Phoenix made their first 25 free throws and nearly set a record for most free throws in a game without a miss until <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jae_Crowder" title="Jae Crowder" id="mwAaE">Jae Crowder</a> missed with 24.8 seconds left in the game. The Suns finished 25 of 26 on their free throws compared to the Bucks' 9 for 16.<sup about="#mwt110" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bontemps_07082021_30-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bontemps_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bontemps_07082021-30" id="mwAaI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaQ">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt113" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-31" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-31"}}'><a href="#cite_note-31" id="mwAaY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAac"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAag">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAak">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt116" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-32" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-32"}}'><a href="#cite_note-32" id="mwAao"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAas"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaw">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAa0">]</span></span></a></sup> The loss by the Bucks marked the third straight series in which they trailed.<sup about="#mwt117" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sopan_07202021_10-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sopan_07202021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sopan_07202021-10" id="mwAa4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAa8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbA">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbE">]</span></span></a></sup> This marked Phoenix' first win at home in the Finals since <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1976_NBA_Finals" title="1976 NBA Finals" id="mwAbI">1976</a>, and the first time they ever held a series lead in the Finals.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwAbM" aria-labelledby="Game_2"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_2">Game 2</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2021_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Game 2"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt118" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAbQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Basketballbox","href":"./Template:Basketballbox"},"params":{"bg":{"wt":"#eee"},"date":{"wt":"July 8"},"time":{"wt":"9:00pm {{small|(6:00pm [[Mountain Standard Time Zone|MST]])}}"},"place":{"wt":"[[Phoenix Suns Arena]], [[Phoenix, Arizona]]"},"TV":{"wt":"[[NBA on ABC|ABC]]"},"team1":{"wt":"[[Milwaukee Bucks]]"},"score1":{"wt":"108"},"team2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;[[Phoenix Suns]]&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"score2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;118&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"report":{"wt":"[https://www.nba.com/game/mil-vs-phx-0042000402 Recap]"},"Q1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;29&apos;&apos;&apos;–26"},"Q2":{"wt":"16–&apos;&apos;&apos;30&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q3":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;33&apos;&apos;&apos;–32"},"Q4":{"wt":"30–30"},"points1":{"wt":"[[Giannis Antetokounmpo]] 42"},"points2":{"wt":"[[Devin Booker]] 31"},"rebounds1":{"wt":"Giannis Antetokounmpo 12"},"rebounds2":{"wt":"[[Deandre Ayton]] 11"},"assist1":{"wt":"[[Khris Middleton]] 8"},"assist2":{"wt":"[[Chris Paul]] 8"},"attendance":{"wt":"16,583"},"referee":{"wt":"*No. 15 [[Zach Zarba]]\n*No. 25 [[Tony Brothers]]\n*No. 4 Sean Wright"},"series":{"wt":"Phoenix leads series, 2–0"}},"i":0}}]}'></div><div style="width: 100%; background-color:#eee; color:#202122;" about="#mwt118" id="mwAbU">
