<table style="background-color:#eee; color:#202122; float:right; width:24%; table-layout:fixed">
<tbody><tr><td style="border-style:none"><div style="font-size:85%"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix_Suns_Arena" title="Phoenix Suns Arena" class="mw-redirect">Phoenix Suns Arena</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix,_Arizona" title="Phoenix, Arizona">Phoenix, Arizona</a><br/><b>Attendance:</b> 16,583<br/><b>Referees:</b> 
<ul><li>No. 15 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zach_Zarba" title="Zach Zarba">Zach Zarba</a></li>
<li>No. 25 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Brothers" title="Tony Brothers">Tony Brothers</a></li>
<li>No. 4 Sean Wright</li></ul></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAbY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Devin_Booker_(30362063153)_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAbc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Devin_Booker_(30362063153)_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Devin_Booker_%2830362063153%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Devin_Booker_%2830362063153%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Devin_Booker_%2830362063153%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Devin_Booker_%2830362063153%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2597" data-file-height="3655" data-file-type="bitmap" height="267" width="190" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwAbg"/></a><figcaption id="mwAbk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devin_Booker" title="Devin Booker" id="mwAbo">Devin Booker</a> led the Suns with 31 points, including seven <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three-point_field_goal" title="Three-point field goal" id="mwAbs">three-pointers</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAbw">Booker scored 31 points and Paul had 23 as the Suns won 118–108 to take a 2–0 series lead. Phoenix made 20 of its 40 three-pointers, including seven makes from Booker.<sup about="#mwt121" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ap_07082021-33"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAb0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAb4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb8">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcA">]</span></span></a></sup> Bridges added 27 points and seven rebounds for the Suns,<sup about="#mwt124" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07092021_11-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07092021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-abrams_07092021-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07092021-11" id="mwAcE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcM">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and Paul also had eight assists.<sup about="#mwt125" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAcU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcc">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcg">]</span></span></a></sup> Antetokounmpo had 42 points and 12 rebounds for Milwaukee.<sup about="#mwt126" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAck"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAco"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcs">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcw">]</span></span></a></sup> Phoenix was up 65–50 towards the start of the third period, but Antetokounmpo scored 20 points in the quarter, including a stretch of 13 consecutive points for the Bucks, to keep his team in the game.<sup about="#mwt127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAc0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAc4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc8">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-34" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-34"}}'><a href="#cite_note-34" id="mwAdE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdM">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAdU">The Bucks outscored the Suns 20–0 in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_(basketball)" title="Key (basketball)" id="mwAdY">key</a> in the opening period, but Phoenix made eight 3-pointers and trailed just 29–26. With less than five minutes remaining in the first half, the game was tied at 41 before Phoenix ended with a 15–4 run.<sup about="#mwt131" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAdc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdk">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdo">]</span></span></a></sup> On their last possession, the Suns made 10 passes, with every team member touching the ball, culminating in Bridges passing the ball to Ayton, who laid it in while being fouled.<sup about="#mwt132" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAds"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd0">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt133" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07092021_11-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07092021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07092021-11" id="mwAd8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeE">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeI">]</span></span></a></sup> Phoenix weathered Antetokounmpo's 20-point quarter in the third, when he joined <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jordan" title="Michael Jordan" id="mwAeM">Michael Jordan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isiah_Thomas" title="Isiah Thomas" id="mwAeQ">Isiah Thomas</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Dumars" title="Joe Dumars" id="mwAeU">Joe Dumars</a> as the other players to score at least 20 in a quarter during a finals game.<sup about="#mwt134" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07092021_11-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07092021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07092021-11" id="mwAeY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAec"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAek">]</span></span></a></sup> Milwaukee cut the lead to six in the fourth quarter, but a 3-pointer by Paul and a basket by Bridges expanded the lead back to double figures,<sup about="#mwt135" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAeo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAes"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAew">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAe0">]</span></span></a></sup> and Booker made three of his 3-point shots to fend off the Bucks.<sup about="#mwt136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07092021_11-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07092021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07092021-11" id="mwAe4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAe8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfA">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAfI">Antetokounmpo had more than twice as many <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Field_goal_(basketball)" title="Field goal (basketball)" id="mwAfM">field goals</a> as any other teammate, shooting 15 for 22 from the field, and 11 for 18 from the free-throw line.<sup about="#mwt137" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07092021_11-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07092021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07092021-11" id="mwAfQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfY">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfc">]</span></span></a></sup> Holiday scored 17 for Milwaukee on just 7-for-21 shooting, and Middleton had 11 points but was 5 for 16.<sup about="#mwt138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAfg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfo">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfs">]</span></span></a></sup> Crowder bounced back from an 0-for-8 shooting performance in Game 1 with 11 points and 10 rebounds for Phoenix.<sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07082021_33-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07082021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07082021-33" id="mwAfw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAf0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf4">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwAgA" aria-labelledby="Game_3"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_3">Game 3</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2021_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Game 3"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt140" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAgE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Basketballbox","href":"./Template:Basketballbox"},"params":{"bg":{"wt":"#eee"},"date":{"wt":"July 11"},"time":{"wt":"8:00pm {{small|(7:00pm [[Central Time Zone|CDT]])}}"},"place":{"wt":"[[Fiserv Forum]], [[Milwaukee|Milwaukee, Wisconsin]]"},"TV":{"wt":"[[NBA on ABC|ABC]]"},"team1":{"wt":"[[Phoenix Suns]]"},"score1":{"wt":"100"},"team2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;[[Milwaukee Bucks]]&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"score2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;120&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"report":{"wt":"[https://www.nba.com/game/phx-vs-mil-0042000403 Recap]"},"Q1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;28&apos;&apos;&apos;–25"},"Q2":{"wt":"17–&apos;&apos;&apos;35&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q3":{"wt":"31–&apos;&apos;&apos;38&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q4":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;24&apos;&apos;&apos;–22"},"points1":{"wt":"[[Chris Paul]] 19"},"points2":{"wt":"[[Giannis Antetokounmpo]] 41"},"rebounds1":{"wt":"[[Deandre Ayton]] 9"},"rebounds2":{"wt":"Giannis Antetokounmpo 13"},"assist1":{"wt":"Chris Paul 9"},"assist2":{"wt":"[[Jrue Holiday]] 9"},"attendance":{"wt":"16,637"},"referee":{"wt":"*No. 48 [[Scott Foster (basketball)|Scott Foster]]\n*No. 42 Eric Lewis\n*No. 60 James Williams"},"series":{"wt":"Phoenix leads series, 2–1"}},"i":0}}]}'></div><div style="width: 100%; background-color:#eee; color:#202122;" about="#mwt140" id="mwAgI">
