<ul><li>No. 19 James Capers</li>
<li>No. 16 David Guthrie</li>
<li>No. 61 Courtney Kirkland</li></ul></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAlE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Khris_Middleton_(39684853532)_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAlI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Khris_Middleton_(39684853532)_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Khris_Middleton_%2839684853532%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Khris_Middleton_%2839684853532%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Khris_Middleton_%2839684853532%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Khris_Middleton_%2839684853532%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2089" data-file-height="1811" data-file-type="bitmap" height="165" width="190" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwAlM"/></a><figcaption id="mwAlQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khris_Middleton" title="Khris Middleton" id="mwAlU">Khris Middleton</a> scored 40 points, including 10 straight in the closing minutes of the game.<sup about="#mwt174" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07142021_42-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07142021-42" id="mwAlY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlg">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlk">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAlo">Middleton scored 40 points, including 10 straight for Milwaukee in the closing moments, and the Bucks won 109–103 to tie the series 2–2. Booker rebounded from his Game 3 struggles to score a game-high 42 points, but his playing time was restricted late by foul trouble.<sup about="#mwt179" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07142021_42-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07142021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-buckner_07142021-42"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07142021-42" id="mwAls"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAl0">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAl4">]</span></span></a></sup> The Suns led for 37:55 of the first 44 minutes of the game.<sup about="#mwt180" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-mcmenamin_07152021_43-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"mcmenamin_07152021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-mcmenamin_07152021-43" id="mwAl8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmE">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmI">]</span></span></a></sup> With 3:42 left in the fourth and the Suns up by three Jrue Holiday attempted a layup and received a great deal of contact from Devin Booker with no call (the play was determined to be a foul by the NBA in the Last 3:30 Report after the game).<sup about="#mwt183" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44"}}'><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mwAmM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmU">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmY">]</span></span></a></sup> If Devin Booker had received the foul, it would have been his sixth, resulting in him being ejected and hugely affecting the game. This sparked a lot of controversy online, with the decision to not call the foul being criticised by fans and sports media.<sup about="#mwt186" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mwAmc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmk">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmo">]</span></span></a></sup> They were up two with <style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1154941027" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt175" id="mwAms" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Fraction/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"frac","href":"./Template:Frac"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2"},"2":{"wt":"1"},"3":{"wt":"2"}},"i":0}}]}'>.mw-parser-output .frac{white-space:nowrap}.mw-parser-output .frac .num,.mw-parser-output .frac .den{font-size:80%;line-height:0;vertical-align:super}.mw-parser-output .frac .den{vertical-align:sub}.mw-parser-output .sr-only{border:0;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);clip-path:polygon(0px 0px,0px 0px,0px 0px);height:1px;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;padding:0;position:absolute;width:1px}</style><span class="frac" about="#mwt175" id="mwAmw">2<span class="sr-only">+</span><span class="num">1</span><span typeof="mw:Entity">⁄</span><span class="den">2</span></span> minutes remaining when Middleton scored the next eight points in the contest.<sup about="#mwt189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bontemps_07142021_46-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bontemps_07142021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-bontemps_07142021-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bontemps_07142021-46" id="mwAm0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAm4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAm8">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt190" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07142021_47-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07142021-47" id="mwAnE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnM">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnQ">]</span></span></a></sup> He made consecutive midrange jump shots to place Milwaukee up for good at 101–99 with 1:28 in the game.<sup about="#mwt191" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bontemps_07142021_46-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bontemps_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bontemps_07142021-46" id="mwAnU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnc">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAng">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt194" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07142021_47-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07142021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ap_07142021-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07142021-47" id="mwAnk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAno"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAns">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnw">]</span></span></a></sup> Jumping off the left leg that he hyperextended two weeks earlier,<sup about="#mwt195" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bontemps_07142021_46-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bontemps_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bontemps_07142021-46" id="mwAn0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAn4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn8">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoA">]</span></span></a></sup> Antetokounmpo blocked a potential game-tying <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alley-oop_(basketball)" title="Alley-oop (basketball)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAoE">alley-oop</a> by Ayton with 1:14 left,<sup about="#mwt196" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07142021_42-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07142021-42" id="mwAoI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoQ">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt197" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07142021_47-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07142021-47" id="mwAoY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAog">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAok">]</span></span></a></sup> prompting fans and media to debate the play's standing among the greatest blocks of all time.<sup about="#mwt200" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-aschburner_07152021_48-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"aschburner_07152021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-aschburner_07152021-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-aschburner_07152021-48" id="mwAoo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAos"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAow">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo0">]</span></span></a></sup>  After Paul lost his balance of his own accord and turned over the ball, Holiday picked up the loose ball and Middleton made a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast-break" title="Fast-break" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAo4">fast-break</a> layup and with 27.2 seconds left for a four-point lead.<sup about="#mwt201" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07142021_42-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07142021-42" id="mwAo8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApE">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-herring_07152021_49-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"herring_07152021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-herring_07152021-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-herring_07152021-49" id="mwApM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApU">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt205" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-golliver_07152021_50-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"golliver_07152021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-golliver_07152021-50" id="mwApc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApk">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApo">]</span></span></a></sup>  He capped off his run with four free throws to bring the score to 107–101.<sup about="#mwt206" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07142021_47-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07142021-47" id="mwAps"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp0">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp4">]</span></span></a></sup> The Bucks outscored the Suns 33–21 in the fourth quarter.<sup about="#mwt209" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-golliver_07152021_50-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"golliver_07152021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-golliver_07152021-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-golliver_07152021-50" id="mwAp8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqE">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqI">]</span></span></a></sup> Antetokounmpo finished with 26 points along with 14 rebounds and eight assists.<sup about="#mwt210" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07142021_47-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07142021-47" id="mwAqM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqU">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAqc">Phoenix made 51.3% of their shots compared to Milwaukee's 40.2%, but they took 19 fewer shots (78–97) due to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turnover_(basketball)" title="Turnover (basketball)" id="mwAqg">turnovers</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Offensive_rebound" title="Offensive rebound" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAqk">offensive rebounds</a>, outperformed by the Bucks 17–5 in both.<sup about="#mwt211" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-aschburner_07152021_48-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"aschburner_07152021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-aschburner_07152021-48" id="mwAqo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqw">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAq0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-mcmenamin_07152021_43-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"mcmenamin_07152021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-mcmenamin_07152021-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-mcmenamin_07152021-43" id="mwAq4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAq8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArA">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArE">]</span></span></a></sup> The Bucks scored 24 points off turnovers,<sup about="#mwt215" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-aschburner_07152021_48-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"aschburner_07152021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-aschburner_07152021-48" id="mwArI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArQ">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArU">]</span></span></a></sup> and their offensive boards led to 19 second-chance points.<sup about="#mwt216" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-mcmenamin_07152021_43-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"mcmenamin_07152021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-mcmenamin_07152021-43" id="mwArY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArg">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArk">]</span></span></a></sup> Crowder scored 15 points for Phoenix, while Paul was held to 10 points on 5–13 shooting and committed five turnovers. Holiday scored 13 on just 4 for 20 shooting, but he added seven rebounds, seven assists and only one turnover, while his defense disrupted Paul.<sup about="#mwt217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07142021_47-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07142021-47" id="mwAro"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArw">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt218" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-herring_07152021_49-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"herring_07152021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-herring_07152021-49" id="mwAr4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAr8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsA">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsE">]</span></span></a></sup> The Bucks also got 14 points from Lopez and 11 points and nine rebounds from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pat_Connaughton" title="Pat Connaughton" id="mwAsI">Pat Connaughton</a>.<sup about="#mwt219" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07142021_47-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07142021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07142021-47" id="mwAsM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsU">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsY">]</span></span></a></sup> Middleton and Antetokounmpo became the third set of teammates to score 40 or more points in games in the same Finals series, joining Abdul-Jabbar and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_Johnson" title="Magic Johnson" id="mwAsc">Magic Johnson</a> with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Lakers" title="Los Angeles Lakers" id="mwAsg">Los Angeles Lakers</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1980_NBA_Finals" title="1980 NBA Finals" id="mwAsk">1980</a>) and LeBron James and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyrie_Irving" title="Kyrie Irving" id="mwAso">Kyrie Irving</a> while with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleveland_Cavaliers" title="Cleveland Cavaliers" id="mwAss">Cleveland Cavaliers</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2016_NBA_Finals" title="2016 NBA Finals" id="mwAsw">2016</a>).<sup about="#mwt222" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwAs0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAs4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAs8">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwAtE" aria-labelledby="Game_5"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_5">Game 5</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2021_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Game 5"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt223" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAtI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Basketballbox","href":"./Template:Basketballbox"},"params":{"bg":{"wt":"#eee"},"date":{"wt":"July 17"},"time":{"wt":"9:00pm {{small|(6:00pm [[Mountain Standard Time Zone|MST]])}}"},"place":{"wt":"[[Footprint Center]], [[Phoenix, Arizona]]"},"TV":{"wt":"[[NBA on ABC|ABC]]"},"team1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;[[Milwaukee Bucks]]&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"score1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;123&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"team2":{"wt":"[[Phoenix Suns]]"},"score2":{"wt":"119"},"report":{"wt":"[https://www.nba.com/game/mil-vs-phx-0042000405 Recap]"},"Q1":{"wt":"21–&apos;&apos;&apos;37&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;43–&apos;&apos;&apos;24"},"Q3":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;36&apos;&apos;&apos;–29"},"Q4":{"wt":"23–&apos;&apos;&apos;29&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"points1":{"wt":"[[Giannis Antetokounmpo]] 32"},"points2":{"wt":"[[Devin Booker]] 40"},"rebounds1":{"wt":"Giannis Antetokounmpo 9"},"rebounds2":{"wt":"[[Deandre Ayton]] 10"},"assist1":{"wt":"[[Jrue Holiday]] 13"},"assist2":{"wt":"[[Chris Paul]] 11"},"attendance":{"wt":"16,562"},"referee":{"wt":"*No. 8 Marc Davis\n*No. 58 Josh Tiven\n*No. 60 James Williams"},"series":{"wt":"Milwaukee leads series, 3–2"}},"i":0}}]}'></div><div style="width: 100%; background-color:#eee; color:#202122;" about="#mwt223" id="mwAtM">
