<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAtQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Jrue_Holiday_2021.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAtU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Jrue_Holiday_2021.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Jrue_Holiday_2021.jpg/250px-Jrue_Holiday_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Jrue_Holiday_2021.jpg/500px-Jrue_Holiday_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1360" data-file-height="1720" data-file-type="bitmap" height="240" width="190" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwAtY"/></a><figcaption id="mwAtc">With about 16 seconds remaining, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jrue_Holiday" title="Jrue Holiday" id="mwAtg">Jrue Holiday</a> stole the ball from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devin_Booker" title="Devin Booker" id="mwAtk">Devin Booker</a> and passed it to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giannis_Antetokounmpo" title="Giannis Antetokounmpo" id="mwAto">Giannis Antetokounmpo</a> for an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alley-oop_(basketball)" title="Alley-oop (basketball)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAts">alley-oop</a>. The Bucks won 123–119.<sup about="#mwt224" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07172021_52-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07172021-52" id="mwAtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAt0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt4">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt8">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAuA">A day before the start of Game 5, the formerly tentatively named <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix_Suns_Arena" title="Phoenix Suns Arena" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAuE">Phoenix Suns Arena</a> would officially receive the new name of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Footprint_Center" title="Footprint Center" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAuI">Footprint Center</a>, which went into effect in time for Game 5 of the NBA Finals to begin. With Milwaukee leading by one with about 16 seconds remaining in the game, Holiday stole the ball from Phoenix's Booker and passed to Antetokounmpo for an alley-oop and a free throw (fouled by Paul on the finish) to secure the game for a 123–119 Bucks' win and a 3–2 series lead.<sup about="#mwt229" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07172021_52-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07172021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-buckner_07172021-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07172021-52" id="mwAuM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuU">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt232" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ap_07172021-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAuc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuk">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuo">]</span></span></a></sup> Milwaukee recovered from an early 16-point deficit to outscore Phoenix 87–57 from the start of the second quarter to around the nine-minute mark of the fourth quarter. The Suns were down 10 with <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1154941027" about="#mwt225" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAus" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Fraction/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"frac","href":"./Template:Frac"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"3"},"2":{"wt":"1"},"3":{"wt":"2"}},"i":0}}]}'/><span class="frac" about="#mwt225" id="mwAuw">3<span class="sr-only">+</span><span class="num">1</span><span typeof="mw:Entity">⁄</span><span class="den">2</span></span> minutes left in the game before a basket by Paul cut it to 120–119 with 56 seconds to play.<sup about="#mwt233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAu0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAu4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu8">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvA">]</span></span></a></sup> Holiday had 27 points, 13 assists and three steals.<sup about="#mwt234" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-brewer_07182021_12-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"brewer_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-brewer_07182021-12" id="mwAvE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvM">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Antetokounmpo had 32 points, nine rebounds, and six assists, and Middleton finished with 29 points.<sup about="#mwt235" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAvU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvc">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvg">]</span></span></a></sup> Booker had a game-high 40 points,<sup about="#mwt236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07172021_52-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07172021-52" id="mwAvk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvs">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvw">]</span></span></a></sup> his second-straight contest with at least 40.<sup about="#mwt237" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAv0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAv4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAv8">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAwE">Phoenix made 14 of 19 shots in the first quarter, including a stretch of 11 straight makes,<sup about="#mwt238" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07172021_52-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07172021-52" id="mwAwI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwQ">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwU">]</span></span></a></sup> and led 37–21 after the first period.<sup about="#mwt239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAwY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwg">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwk">]</span></span></a></sup> However, Milwaukee outscored them 21–5 to open the second quarter, tying the game at 42 on a 3-pointer by Connaughton with 7:48 left in the half.<sup about="#mwt240" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAwo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAws"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAww">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAw0">]</span></span></a></sup> Holiday scored 14 in the quarter,<sup about="#mwt241" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAw4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAw8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxA">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxE">]</span></span></a></sup> when the Bucks scored a record 43 points in a quarter by a road team in the Finals, and they led 64–61 at halftime.<sup about="#mwt242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07172021_52-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07172021-52" id="mwAxI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxQ">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxU">]</span></span></a></sup> After three quarters, the Bucks had made 62.1% of their shots, rivaling <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orlando_Magic" title="Orlando Magic" id="mwAxY">Orlando</a>'s single-game Finals record of 62.5% in Game 3 of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_NBA_Finals" title="2009 NBA Finals" id="mwAxc">2009 finals</a> against the Lakers. Milwaukee led 108–94 after a basket by Holiday with about nine minutes remaining in the game, but the Suns mounted their comeback to pull within one in the final minute.<sup about="#mwt243" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAxg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxo">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxs">]</span></span></a></sup> After a Holiday miss, Booker rebounded the ball and dribbled it upcourt himself. He stopped and pivoted in the paint, when Holiday forcefully pulled the ball from his hands for the steal.<sup about="#mwt244" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-naokarni_07182021_54-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"naokarni_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-naokarni_07182021-54" id="mwAxw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAx0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAx4">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAx8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07182021_55-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07182021-55" id="mwAyA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyI">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyM">]</span></span></a></sup> After initially intending to run down the clock,<sup about="#mwt248" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-devine_07182021_56-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"devine_07182021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-devine_07182021-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-devine_07182021-56" id="mwAyQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyY">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyc">]</span></span></a></sup> Holiday instead passed it for the dunk by Antetokounmpo, who was begging for the ball.<sup about="#mwt251" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-naokarni_07182021_54-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"naokarni_07182021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-naokarni_07182021-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-naokarni_07182021-54" id="mwAyg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyo">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAys">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt254" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07182021_55-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07182021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-abrams_07182021-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07182021-55" id="mwAyw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAy0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAy4">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAy8">]</span></span></a></sup> Fouled on the play by Paul, Antetokounmpo missed the free throw,<sup about="#mwt255" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07172021_53-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07172021-53" id="mwAzA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzI">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzM">]</span></span></a></sup> making just 4 of 11 in the game.<sup about="#mwt256" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-devine_07182021_56-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"devine_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-devine_07182021-56" id="mwAzQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzY">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzc">]</span></span></a></sup> However, he volleyed the ball for an offensive rebound by Middleton, who made one of two free throws for the final score of the game.<sup about="#mwt257" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07182021_55-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07182021-55" id="mwAzg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzo">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAzw">Milwaukee became the first team in the series to win on the road.<sup about="#mwt258" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07172021_52-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07172021-52" id="mwAz0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAz4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAz8">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0A">]</span></span></a></sup> Antetokounmpo, Holiday, and Middleton combined for 88 points, becoming the fifth trio to each score 25 points on 50% shooting in a single Finals game, and the first to accomplish the feat since the Lakers' Abdul-Jabbar (36 points), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Worthy" title="James Worthy" id="mwA0E">James Worthy</a> (33), and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_Johnson" title="Magic Johnson" id="mwA0I">Magic Johnson</a> (26) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1985_NBA_Finals" title="1985 NBA Finals" id="mwA0M">1985</a>.<sup about="#mwt261" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nba_07182021_57-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nba_07182021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-nba_07182021-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nba_07182021-57" id="mwA0Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0Y">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0c">]</span></span></a></sup> Phoenix lost three straight games for only the second time in the season, the first occurring six months earlier.<sup about="#mwt262" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-devine_07182021_56-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"devine_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-devine_07182021-56" id="mwA0g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0o">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0s">]</span></span></a></sup> Paul ended the game with 21 points, 11 assists and one turnover,<sup about="#mwt263" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abrams_07182021_55-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abrams_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abrams_07182021-55" id="mwA0w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA00"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA04">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA08">]</span></span></a></sup> while Ayton finished with 20 points and 10 rebounds. Booker became the first player in the Finals to score at least 40 in consecutive games and lose both.<sup about="#mwt264" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-naokarni_07182021_54-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"naokarni_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-naokarni_07182021-54" id="mwA1A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1I">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1M">]</span></span></a></sup> Antetokounmpo and he were the first pair of players to score 40+ twice in the same Finals.<sup about="#mwt265" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nba_07182021_57-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nba_07182021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nba_07182021-57" id="mwA1Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1Y">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1c">]</span></span></a></sup> Bucks' role player <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thanasis_Antetokounmpo" title="Thanasis Antetokounmpo" id="mwA1g">Thanasis Antetokounmpo</a>, the older brother of Giannis, and assistant coach <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Oppenheimer" title="Josh Oppenheimer" id="mwA1k">Josh Oppenheimer</a> were away from the team due to COVID-19 health and safety protocols. The NBA also replaced referee Sean Wright after he entered health and safety protocols.<sup about="#mwt266" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buckner_07172021_52-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"buckner_07172021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-buckner_07172021-52" id="mwA1o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1w">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA10">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwA14" aria-labelledby="Game_6"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_6">Game 6</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2021_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: Game 6"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt267" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA18" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Basketballbox","href":"./Template:Basketballbox"},"params":{"bg":{"wt":"#eee"},"date":{"wt":"July 20"},"time":{"wt":"9:00pm {{small|(8:00pm [[Central Time Zone|CDT]])}}"},"place":{"wt":"[[Fiserv Forum]], [[Milwaukee|Milwaukee, Wisconsin]]"},"TV":{"wt":"[[NBA on ABC|ABC]]"},"team1":{"wt":"[[Phoenix Suns]]"},"score1":{"wt":"98"},"team2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;[[Milwaukee Bucks]]&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"score2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;105&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"report":{"wt":"[https://www.nba.com/game/phx-vs-mil-0042000406 Recap]"},"Q1":{"wt":"16–&apos;&apos;&apos;29&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;31&apos;&apos;&apos;–13"},"Q3":{"wt":"30–&apos;&apos;&apos;35&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q4":{"wt":"21–&apos;&apos;&apos;28&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"points1":{"wt":"[[Chris Paul]] 26"},"points2":{"wt":"[[Giannis Antetokounmpo]] 50"},"rebounds1":{"wt":"[[Jae Crowder]] 13"},"rebounds2":{"wt":"Giannis Antetokounmpo 14"},"assist1":{"wt":"[[Devin Booker|Booker]], Paul 5 each"},"assist2":{"wt":"[[Jrue Holiday]] 11"},"attendance":{"wt":"17,397"},"referee":{"wt":"*No. 48 [[Scott Foster (basketball)|Scott Foster]]\n*No. 42 Eric Lewis\n*No. 25 [[Tony Brothers]]"},"series":{"wt":"Milwaukee wins NBA Finals, 4–2"}},"i":0}}]}'></div><div style="width: 100%; background-color:#eee; color:#202122;" about="#mwt267" id="mwA2A">
