</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwA2E"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Giannis_Antetokounmpo_(24845003687)_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwA2I"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Giannis_Antetokounmpo_(24845003687)_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Giannis_Antetokounmpo_%2824845003687%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Giannis_Antetokounmpo_%2824845003687%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Giannis_Antetokounmpo_%2824845003687%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Giannis_Antetokounmpo_%2824845003687%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2199" data-file-height="2839" data-file-type="bitmap" height="245" width="190" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwA2M"/></a><figcaption id="mwA2Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giannis_Antetokounmpo" title="Giannis Antetokounmpo" id="mwA2U">Giannis Antetokounmpo</a> was named the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Finals_Most_Valuable_Player_Award" title="NBA Finals Most Valuable Player Award" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA2Y">Finals MVP</a>, scoring 50 points in Game 6.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwA2c">Giannis Antetokounmpo scored a playoff career-high 50 points and added 14 rebounds and five blocks to lead the Bucks to a 105–98 victory to win the series in six games.<sup about="#mwt270" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sopan_07202021_10-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sopan_07202021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-sopan_07202021-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sopan_07202021-10" id="mwA2g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2o">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2s">]</span></span></a></sup> The 50 points tied a Finals record for the most scored by a player in a series-clinching game, set by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bob_Pettit" title="Bob Pettit" id="mwA2w">Bob Pettit</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Louis_Hawks" title="St. Louis Hawks" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA20">St. Louis Hawks</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1958_NBA_Finals" title="1958 NBA Finals" id="mwA24">1958</a>.<sup about="#mwt273" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pettit_58-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Pettit"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pettit-58"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Pettit-58" id="mwA28"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3E">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3I">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt276" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwA3M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3U">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3Y">]</span></span></a></sup> After his dominant performance in the series, including his third game with at least 40 points and 10 rebounds, Antetokounmpo was named the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Finals_Most_Valuable_Player_Award" title="NBA Finals Most Valuable Player Award" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA3c">Finals MVP</a>,<sup about="#mwt277" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07202021_60-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07202021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07202021-60" id="mwA3g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3o">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3s">]</span></span></a></sup> the youngest winner at age 26 since <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kawhi_Leonard" title="Kawhi Leonard" id="mwA3w">Kawhi Leonard</a> (22) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_NBA_Finals" title="2014 NBA Finals" id="mwA30">2014</a>.<sup about="#mwt280" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61"}}'><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwA34"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA38"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4A">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4E">]</span></span></a></sup> Antetokounmpo made 16 of his 25 shots, and was a surprising 17 for 19 on his free throws after hitting just 55.6% in the playoffs. The game was tied at 77 after three quarters before he scored 13 in the final period to lead Milwaukee to its first championship since <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1970–71_Milwaukee_Bucks_season" title="1970–71 Milwaukee Bucks season" id="mwA4I">1971</a>, when they were led by Abdul-Jabbar and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscar_Robertson" title="Oscar Robertson" id="mwA4M">Oscar Robertson</a>. Paul led the Suns with 26 points.<sup about="#mwt283" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07202021_60-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07202021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ap_07202021-60"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07202021-60" id="mwA4Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA4U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4Y">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4c">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwA4g">Middleton scored 17 and reserve <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobby_Portis" title="Bobby Portis" id="mwA4k">Bobby Portis</a> added 16 for the Bucks. Holiday had 12 points, 11 assists, and nine rebounds. His defense helped limit Booker to 19 points on just 8-for-22 shooting, missing all seven of his 3-point attempts. Milwaukee became the fifth team <span class="citation-needed-content" style="padding-left:0.1em; padding-right:0.1em; color:var(--color-subtle, #54595d); border:1px solid var(--border-color-subtle, #c8ccd1);" about="#mwt284" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA4o" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Citation needed span","href":"./Template:Citation_needed_span"},"params":{"text":{"wt":"(after the [[1968–69 Boston Celtics season|1969 Boston Celtics]], [[1976–77 Portland Trail Blazers season|1977 Portland Trail Blazers]], [[2005–06 Miami Heat season|2006 Miami Heat]], and [[2015–16 Cleveland Cavaliers season|2016 Cleveland Cavaliers]])"},"date":{"wt":"July 2022"}},"i":0}}]}'>(after the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968–69_Boston_Celtics_season" title="1968–69 Boston Celtics season">1969 Boston Celtics</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1976–77_Portland_Trail_Blazers_season" title="1976–77 Portland Trail Blazers season">1977 Portland Trail Blazers</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2005–06_Miami_Heat_season" title="2005–06 Miami Heat season">2006 Miami Heat</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2015–16_Cleveland_Cavaliers_season" title="2015–16 Cleveland Cavaliers season">2016 Cleveland Cavaliers</a>)</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt284"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_July_2022" about="#mwt284"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="margin-left:0.1em; white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt284" id="mwA4s"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (July 2022)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> to come back from a 2–0 deficit in the Finals, and the first to do so by winning the next four games since <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miami_Heat" title="Miami Heat" id="mwA4w">Miami</a> defeated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dallas_Mavericks" title="Dallas Mavericks" id="mwA40">Dallas</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2006_NBA_Finals" title="2006 NBA Finals" id="mwA44">2006</a>.<sup about="#mwt285" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07202021_60-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07202021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07202021-60" id="mwA48"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5E">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5I">]</span></span></a></sup> They also became the second team in NBA history to come back from down 2–0 twice in the same playoffs after the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020–21_Los_Angeles_Clippers_season" title="2020–21 Los Angeles Clippers season" id="mwA5M">2020–21 Los Angeles Clippers</a> also did so in consecutive rounds.<sup about="#mwt288" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62"}}'><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwA5Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5Y">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5c">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt291" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwA5g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5o">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5s">]</span></span></a></sup> The Suns have won two games in each of their three Finals appearances.<sup about="#mwt292" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_07202021_60-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_07202021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_07202021-60" id="mwA5w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA50"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA54">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA58">]</span></span></a></sup> Paul became the first player in NBA playoff history to lose four series in which his team led 2–0.<sup about="#mwt295" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-64" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-64"}}'><a href="#cite_note-64" id="mwA6A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6I">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6M">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt296" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA6Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"clear","href":"./Template:Clear"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwA6U" aria-labelledby="Rosters"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Rosters">Rosters</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2021_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: Rosters"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
