</section><section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwA7w" aria-labelledby="Sponsorship"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Sponsorship">Sponsorship</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2021_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19" title="Edit section: Sponsorship"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwA70">As part of a multiyear partnership since 2018, the internet television service <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube_TV" title="YouTube TV" id="mwA74">YouTube TV</a> was the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Title_sponsor" title="Title sponsor" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA78">presenting sponsor</a> of the NBA Finals.<sup about="#mwt375" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-66" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-66"}}'><a href="#cite_note-66" id="mwA8A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8I">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8M">]</span></span></a></sup> YouTube TV introduced a new multi-platform ad campaign during the series featuring a grandmother using the service to watch NBA games on-demand.<sup about="#mwt378" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-67" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-67"}}'><a href="#cite_note-67" id="mwA8Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8Y">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8c">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="20" id="mwA8g" aria-labelledby="Media_coverage"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Media_coverage">Media coverage</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2021_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20" title="Edit section: Media coverage"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwA8k">The Finals were televised in the United States by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_on_ABC" title="NBA on ABC" id="mwA8o">ABC</a> (which included local affiliates <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KNXV-TV" title="KNXV-TV" id="mwA8s">KNXV-TV</a> in Phoenix and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WISN-TV" title="WISN-TV" id="mwA8w">WISN-TV</a> in Milwaukee) for the 19th consecutive year, and broadcast through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_on_ESPN_Radio" title="NBA on ESPN Radio" id="mwA80">ESPN Radio</a> nationally.<sup about="#mwt382" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-68"}}'><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwA84"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA88"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9A">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9E">]</span></span></a></sup> Each of the games' intro videos were directed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spike_Lee" title="Spike Lee" id="mwA9I">Spike Lee</a>.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt379" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9M" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"October 2021"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_October_2021" about="#mwt379"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt379" id="mwA9Q"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (October 2021)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></p>

<p id="mwA9U">As with the previous years, the series was called by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Breen" title="Mike Breen" id="mwA9Y">Mike Breen</a> on play-by-play with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Jackson" title="Mark Jackson" id="mwA9c">Mark Jackson</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Van_Gundy" title="Jeff Van Gundy" id="mwA9g">Jeff Van Gundy</a> as analysts. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rachel_Nichols_(journalist)" title="Rachel Nichols (journalist)" id="mwA9k">Rachel Nichols</a> was originally to be the sideline reporter, but <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malika_Andrews" title="Malika Andrews" id="mwA9o">Malika Andrews</a> took over due to a leaked audio of Nichols saying racist comments against <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Taylor_(sportscaster)" title="Maria Taylor (sportscaster)" id="mwA9s">Maria Taylor</a>.<sup about="#mwt385" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-69" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-69"}}'><a href="#cite_note-69" id="mwA9w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA90"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA94">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA98">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="21" id="mwA-A" aria-labelledby="Viewership"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Viewership">Viewership</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2021_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21" title="Edit section: Viewership"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt386" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-E" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"NBA Finals television ratings"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt387" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt386" id="mwA-I">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Finals_television_ratings" title="NBA Finals television ratings">NBA Finals television ratings</a></div>

