mp;rft.aulast=Steele&amp;rft.aufirst=Ben&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jsonline.com%2Fstory%2Fsports%2Fnba%2Fbucks%2F2021%2F07%2F10%2Fmilwaukee-bucks-vs-phoenix-suns-game-3-nba-finals-chat-updates%2F7917534002%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2021+NBA+Finals" class="Z3988" about="#mwt162" id="mwBes"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-40" id="cite_note-40" data-mw-footnote-number="40"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwBew"><a href="#cite_ref-40" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwBe0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwBe4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-40" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt167" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBe8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"first":{"wt":"Michael C."},"last":{"wt":"Wright"},"title":{"wt":"Finals MVP Ladder: Giannis Antetokounmpo powers his way to the top after Game 3"},"date":{"wt":"July 13, 2021"},"website":{"wt":"NBA.com"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.nba.com/news/finals-mvp-ladder-giannis-antetokounmpo-powers-his-way-to-the-top-after-game-3"},"access-date":{"wt":"July 14, 2021"},"quote":{"wt":"Antetokounmpo scored 42 points to go with 12 rebounds in that Game 2 loss, and in Game 3 all his points came from either inside the paint or at the free throw line, where he had struggled over the first two games in Phoenix as Suns fans threw off his concentration by raucously chanting a count with every attempt."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFWright2021" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt167">Wright, Michael C. (July 13, 2021). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nba.com/news/finals-mvp-ladder-giannis-antetokounmpo-powers-his-way-to-the-top-after-game-3" class="external text" id="mwBfA">"Finals MVP Ladder: Giannis Antetokounmpo powers his way to the top after Game 3"</a>. <i id="mwBfE">NBA.com</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwBfI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwBfM">July 14,</span> 2021</span>. <q id="mwBfQ">Antetokounmpo scored 42 points to go with 12 rebounds in that Game 2 loss, and in Game 3 all his points came from either inside the paint or at the free throw line, where he had struggled over the first two games in Phoenix as Suns fans threw off his concentration by raucously chanting a count with every attempt.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=NBA.com&amp;rft.atitle=Finals+MVP+Ladder%3A+Giannis+Antetokounmpo+powers+his+way+to+the+top+after+Game+3&amp;rft.date=2021-07-13&amp;rft.aulast=Wright&amp;rft.aufirst=Michael+C.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nba.com%2Fnews%2Ffinals-mvp-ladder-giannis-antetokounmpo-powers-his-way-to-the-top-after-game-3&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2021+NBA+Finals" class="Z3988" about="#mwt167" id="mwBfU"></span></span></li>
